 Inc. in February 2021. Alpha Metallurgical Resources, Inc. was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Bristol, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles Andrew Eidson | CEO, Treasurer & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $552K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Alpha Metallurgical Resources,  is a small-cap basic materials business with a $1.9B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -20% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 46% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 37-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $18M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -20.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 30% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom deci